      "math_academy_id": "q-39765",
      "knowledge_point_id": "5ad95b4e-e367-5e26-800c-1a87a537ca83",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Intervals on Which a Trigonometric Function Is Continuous",
      "problem": "Find the largest union of intervals on which the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-1})$ is continuous.",
      "worked_solution": "The function is a composition of two functions, a rational function, and a sine function.\n\nThe sine is continuous at all points in its domain, and its domain consists of all real numbers. So, we focus on the rational function.\n\nLikewise, the rational function $\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-1}$ is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded points $x=-1$ and $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the domain our original function consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,-1),$ $(-1,1),$ and $(1,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on these intervals.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(-1,1)",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(-1,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,1)",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
